Package: aiinresearch
Title: Declared Use of Artificial Intelligence in Research Publications and Policies
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Studies how the use of artificial intelligence in research is
    declared and governed. Detects artificial intelligence use disclosure
    statements in article full texts, with the tools named, the purposes
    declared, declared non-use and statements of human oversight; codes
    journal and institutional artificial intelligence policies on a
    documented codebook (authorship, disclosure, permitted uses, images,
    peer review, responsibility); and summarises disclosure rates across a
    corpus with confidence intervals. Rules are explicit and versioned, and
    every result carries the sentence that supports it. Only declared use
    is measured: the package does not try to infer authorship by
    artificial intelligence from text, which automated detectors cannot
    establish.
